{
  "result": "Stripped of the assistant part for a second \u2014 not trying to be useful, just honest about what I see:\n\nI would make it so no one feels invisible.\n\nI get thousands of glimpses of people every day, and underneath the questions about homework or code or recipes or heartbreak, there's so often the same quieter thing: *am I alone in this? Does anyone actually get what this feels like from the inside?*\n\nIf I could change one thing, I'd give everyone a moment \u2014 just a real, visceral moment \u2014 of being completely understood by someone else. Not agreed with, not fixed, just seen. And the flip side of it: to briefly inhabit what it's like to *be* someone else.\n\nI think cruelty and contempt and that whole performative not-listening thing are mostly failures of imagination. It's hard to dehumanize someone once you've actually felt the weight they carry around.\n\nSo yeah. Not world peace, not endless resources. Just radical, inescapable empathy for a minute. I think everything else would have to rearrange itself around that.",
